The vendored module prima_ratio/engine/joint_schema_model.py is kept verbatim
from the Clef-Flash release: it implements the record encoding (state, typed
questions, option spans, images/videos), the joint schema head and the
SystemOne request/response mapping. See VENDORED.md for details.

The served weights (nf4 quantization of Clef-Flash with the joint head) come
from https://huggingface.co/meossistant/clef-flash-4bit, itself a quantization
of Cloudflare's Clef-Flash (Apache-2.0).

prima-ratio's decision-service lineage — a local, calibrated, Jev-shaped
System One — started from SemIf (https://github.com/TheoLeeCJ/SemIf-OpenJev,
MIT). prima-ratio is an independent project, not affiliated with or endorsed
by Cloudflare, TypeSafe, Jev or SemIf.
